---
title: ALPR Subsystem — Plate Detection and OCR Pipeline
---
flowchart TD
    A[Camera frame captured\n1080p+ RGB] --> B[Preprocess:\nresize, normalize\nOpenCV CUDA]

    B --> C[YOLOv9 Plate Detection\nTensorRT engine\nsm_120 / sm_89]

    C --> D{Plate detected?\nconf >= threshold}
    D -- No --> E[Return: NO_PLATE\nconf=0.0]
    D -- Yes, 1+ plates --> F[For each detected plate]

    F --> G[Crop plate ROI\nfrom original frame]
    G --> H[Perspective rectification\n- deskew tilted plates -\nOpenCV warpPerspective]
    H --> I[Enhance:\nCLAHE contrast\nGaussian denoise\nOpenCV CUDA]

    I --> J[PaddleOCR\nTensorRT engine\ncharacter recognition]

    J --> K[Raw OCR text]
    K --> L[Normalize plate string:\n- Strip spaces/hyphens\n- Uppercase\n- Kenyan format validation\n  KAA 000A / KDG 000A]

    L --> M{Valid Kenyan\nplate format?}
    M -- Yes --> N[Return: plate_text\n+ detection_conf\n+ ocr_conf\n+ plate_image_crop]
    M -- No --> O[Return: INVALID_FORMAT\nraw_text + conf\nfor manual review]

    E --> P[Result to\nDecision Fusion]
    N --> P
    O --> P

    style C fill:#4a9eff,color:#fff
    style J fill:#4a9eff,color:#fff
    style N fill:#16a34a,color:#fff
    style E fill:#dc2626,color:#fff
    style O fill:#f59e0b,color:#fff
